# Sinfonia No. 8 in F major, BWV 794 (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: light and cheerful 4/4. The subject is a quick sixteenth
# turn and leaping eighths (C A D C Bb A G C D Bb C), first heard over a
# held F in the bass. Two-voice passages alternate with full three-part
# writing, which suggests a change of manual.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 72. 23 bars of 4/4 is 92 quarters. Leonhardt
# (harpsichord) takes 1:25, about 65 to the quarter; Schiff (Decca) 1:03,
# about 88. 72 lies between them, toward Leonhardt, so the sixteenths stay
# clear on the chip.
#
# Structure (bars as in the MIDI and score):
#   1      subject in the alto over a bass pedal F (soprano silent)
#   2      soprano answers on F
#   3      bass enters
#   4-6    short imitations of the head
#   7      cadence in C major (beat 3); bass starts the subject at 7.75
#   8-10   two-voice episode (alto silent), sequence toward D minor
#   10.5   alto re-enters with the head, G minor
#   11     cadence in G minor
#   12-13  subject in the bass
#   15     cadence in D minor (beat 3)
#   16     cadence on F, leading into B-flat
#   17-19  B-flat section over a long bass B-flat; subject in the soprano
#          (18), then the bass (19)
#   20     rising sequence, octave leaps in the bass
#   21     the subject back in the bass in F, soprano at its high G
#   22-23  final cadence in F

tempo 72

dyn 1 mf          # bars 1-7: the exposition, bright
dyn 8 mp          # bars 8-11: two-voice episode after the C major
                  # cadence, an echo on the softer manual
dyn 12 mf         # bars 12-16: full texture again after the G minor
                  # cadence, subject in the bass
dyn 17 mp         # bars 17-19: B-flat section, gentler colour
ramp 20 f         # bar 20: the rising sequence builds to the return;
                  # f then holds through bars 21-23, the subject home in F

lead 1 top        # bar 1: alto subject (soprano silent, so it ranks top)
lead 2 top        # bar 2: soprano answer
lead 3 bottom     # bar 3: bass entry
lead 7.75-8 bottom # bars 7.75-8: bass takes the subject after the cadence
lead 10.5-11 mid  # bars 10.5-11: alto re-enters with the head
lead 12 bottom    # bar 12: bass, after the G minor cadence
lead 18 top       # bar 18: soprano, B-flat
lead 19 bottom    # bar 19: bass
lead 21 bottom    # bar 21: bass, the subject's return in F

rit 1.5 0.7       # from the middle of bar 22: the cadential bass line
                  # and the final F with its fermata
